---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How Precision Solutions Tech (SG TECHNOLOGY LLC) handles privacy for our website, developer APIs, automation workflows, and macOS apps including Twinkeep.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-08-25',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/legal/privacy/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li>Privacy Policy</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: August 25, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by
        <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”), handles information when you use
        our website, developer APIs, automation workflows, and macOS apps (including
        <a href="/apps/twinkeep/">Twinkeep</a>).
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also use this page as our <strong>privacy choices</strong> notice: we do not sell
        personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>macOS apps</strong> such as Twinkeep are designed to process files
          <em>on your Mac</em>. Core features do not require uploading your media to our servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>APIs and workflows</strong> are built to be stateless where practical: request
          data is processed to fulfill the call and is not retained as a customer media library.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>This website</strong> may use standard hosting, analytics, or advertising tags
          as described below.
        </li>
        <li>We do <strong>not sell</strong> your personal information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Precision Solutions Tech is the public brand of <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
        Website: <a href="https://precisionsolutionstech.com/">precisionsolutionstech.com</a>.
        Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@precisionsolutionstech.com">hello@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
        or <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="apps">macOS apps (Twinkeep and similar)</h2>
      <p>
        Our Mac apps process content you choose on your device. For Twinkeep specifically, that may
        include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Paths and metadata of files in folders you select (name, size, dates, media type)</li>
        <li>Content fingerprints (hashes) computed locally to detect duplicates</li>
        <li>Thumbnails or previews generated locally for display</li>
        <li>Settings stored in local preferences</li>
        <li>Quarantine / File Rules records stored under your user Application Support folder</li>
        <li>
          Optional Stability monitor samples (approximate per-app CPU and memory, thermal state,
          timestamps) stored only on your Mac for a limited period while that monitor is running
        </li>
        <li>
          Paths and timestamps of local macOS DiagnosticReports that a Stability utility may list —
          read on-device, not uploaded by the app for that purpose
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This processing stays on your device unless you independently copy, share, or sync files
        (for example via your own cloud storage).
      </p>
      <h3>Purchases and support</h3>
      <p>
        If you buy through the Mac App Store, Apple’s terms and privacy policy govern payment. If
        you buy through Gumroad, our website checkout, or another storefront, that storefront’s
        privacy policy governs payment card data (we do not receive your full card number). We may
        receive your name, email, purchase status, and support message content as needed to fulfill
        the purchase, deliver a license, or reply.
      </p>
      <h3>Analytics and ads in the apps</h3>
      <p>
        Current Twinkeep builds do not include third-party advertising SDKs and do not sell personal
        information. If that changes, we will update this policy before shipping the change.
      </p>

      <h2 id="website">Website</h2>
      <p>
        When you visit precisionsolutionstech.com, our hosts and tools may process standard
        technical data such as IP address, browser type, pages viewed, and approximate location
        derived from IP, plus cookies or similar technologies used for security, preferences, or
        measurement. We may use advertising or analytics tags (for example Google tags) on the site;
        those providers process data under their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="apis">Developer APIs and automation workflows</h2>
      <p>
        API and workflow products are generally designed for privacy-first, short-lived processing:
        you send a request, we return a result, and we do not keep your payload as a long-term
        content archive. Marketplace partners (such as RapidAPI or Gumroad) and your own automation
        credentials are governed by those parties’ policies and your configuration. Server logs may
        briefly include technical metadata needed to operate and secure the service.
      </p>

      <h2 id="choices">Your privacy choices</h2>
      <p>
        This section is our notice for “user privacy choices” / “do not sell or share” style
        requests (including California and similar laws, where they apply):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We do <strong>not sell</strong> personal information.</li>
        <li>
          We do <strong>not share</strong> personal information for cross-context behavioral
          advertising in our Mac apps.
        </li>
        <li>
          For Twinkeep: only select folders you intend to scan; disable auto-quarantine if you
          prefer; restore or delete quarantined items; leave optional monitors off; uninstall the
          app to stop local processing.
        </li>
        <li>
          To request access, correction, or deletion of purchase/support records we hold, email
          <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
          with enough detail for us to locate your request. We may need to verify your identity.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="children">Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our products are not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your
        jurisdiction).
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Local app data remains on your Mac until you remove it or uninstall. Purchase and support
        records are retained as needed for accounting, fraud prevention, legal obligations, and
        customer support. Website/server logs are retained for a limited operational period.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use
        after an update means you accept the revised policy for subsequent use.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
        ·
        <a href="mailto:hello@precisionsolutionstech.com">hello@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Product page:
        <a href="/apps/twinkeep/">Twinkeep</a>
        · Company:
        <a href="/about/">About us</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
